# Remediation push cadence

During the `remediation` branch run, **do not push to remote after every prompt**.

## Push rule

- **Commit locally after every prompt** (one prompt, one commit — unchanged).
- **Push to remote only after every 5 completed prompts**, or when the user explicitly asks.
- Track progress in `PROGRESS.md` under **Git push cadence**:
  - `Last push after prompt:` (prompt id or `never`)
  - `Prompts since last push:` (count and ids)
  - `Next push after prompt:` (the 5th prompt in the current batch)

When the counter reaches 5, push with `git push -u origin remediation` (or the current branch), then reset the counter and update `PROGRESS.md`.

## Deploy rule

- **Do not deploy to Vercel after every prompt.**
- Deploy when the user asks, or at the end of a 5-prompt batch if they want preview/production updated then.
- A local commit is not blocked by skipping push; only push/deploy are batched.

## Example

Prompts 11, 12a, 12b, 12c, 13 complete → commit each locally → on completing 13 (5th since last push), push and optionally deploy.
